    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d462">

                <pb facs="0530" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg426"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4379: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-24T15:00:00+01:00">February 24, 1932—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 24—9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. Addendum to my 35. Sato also mentioned their growing feeling of apprehension
                    at the isolation in which Japan found itself and their especial anxiety caused
                    by the evidences of changing sentiment in the United States as shown by the
                    desire of peaceable-minded people to advocate an economic boycott.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
